  "articleBody": "It's frustrating when you see AI overviews and answer engines citing other businesses, but yours is nowhere to be found. Many personal injury firms invest in SEO but miss the crucial differences AI systems look for. Traditional SEO often focuses on keywords and getting on the first page, but AI models, like Google AI Overviews or ChatGPT, prioritize structured data and content that directly answers specific questions. If your website has thin, outdated FAQs, relies on heavy CMS themes that slow down AI crawlers, or lacks proper JSON-LD schema, AI systems will struggle to understand and cite your expertise. They're looking for clear, concise, fact-dense answers, presented in a way that's easy for machines to consume. If your current setup isn't meeting these specific requirements, you're likely missing out on valuable AI visibility.\n\n**Common Mistakes to Avoid**\nMany firms assume that simply having an FAQ section is enough, or that using generic AI content will work. But AI systems need content that is highly structured, semantically relevant, and often goes beyond what's typically found on a standard website. Relying on unreviewed generated text or making structured data claims that aren't visible on the page are common missteps. Also, prioritizing keyword stuffing over genuine answers will hinder your AI visibility. These systems are designed to identify and cite authoritative sources that directly address user queries, not just those with high keyword density. Ignoring the technical aspects of crawlability and structured data specifically for AI systems will consistently leave your firm out of AI citations.\n\nReady to get your personal injury firm cited by leading AI search engines? We can help turn your expertise into machine-readable, answer-ready content.",
